---
import PageLayout from "@layouts/PageLayout.astro";
import { buildPageMetadata } from "@lib/metadata/pageMetadata";

const metadata = buildPageMetadata({
  title: "About Bashir Salami — Hands-on Technical Leader",
  description: "A cross-disciplinary software engineer and technical leader working across product, systems, data, cloud, and operations.",
  path: "/about/"
});
---

<PageLayout
  metadata={metadata}
  eyebrow="About"
  title="Hands-on software engineering and technical leadership."
  summary="Work across frontend development, backend systems, cloud and platform engineering, data infrastructure, and technical architecture."
>
  <section class="reading-shell mdx-content about-content">
    <p>The through-line is work where product behavior depends on deeper system choices: a user workflow tied to a difficult domain model, a data pipeline that changes product behavior, or deployment and observability constraints that shape architecture.</p>
    <p>The work stays close to code, infrastructure, data, design decisions, incident investigation, and code review. Technical leadership is treated as a way to create enough clarity for sound decisions and reliable delivery, not as distance from implementation.</p>
    <h2>Working approach</h2>
    <p>Explicit boundaries, typed contracts, accessible interfaces, observable behavior, and explainable trade-offs matter more than adding technology for its own sake.</p>
  </section>
</PageLayout>
